From: Wendy Labs <engineering@wendy.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] NAN: accept unselected candidate NDC in NDL Request

Upstream-Status: Pending

The Pixel 7 proposes an unselected NDC in its initial NDP Request. A
responder may choose its own selected NDC in the Response. Validate the
candidate's schedule encoding, leave the selected NDC fields empty, and
continue through the existing availability and schedule negotiation.
Responses and Confirms continue to require a selected NDC. Check the
attribute length before reading the control field.

Fix the module-test cleanup to unlink each queued action, rather than a
stale device pointer, so the full NAN regression suite can finish. This
cleanup is only compiled into test builds.

diff --git a/src/nan/nan_i.h b/src/nan/nan_i.h
index 5a9f2b5..978f6d3 100644
--- a/src/nan/nan_i.h
+++ b/src/nan/nan_i.h
@@ -732,6 +732,9 @@ void nan_ndl_setup_failure(struct nan_data *nan, struct nan_peer *peer,
 void nan_ndl_reset(struct nan_data *nan, struct nan_peer *peer);
 int nan_ndl_handle_ndl_attr(struct nan_data *nan, struct nan_peer *peer,
 			    struct nan_msg *msg);
+#ifdef CONFIG_MODULE_TESTS
+int nan_ndl_test_ndc_attrs(void);
+#endif /* CONFIG_MODULE_TESTS */
 int nan_ndl_add_ndl_attr(struct nan_data *nan, const struct nan_peer *peer,
 			 struct wpabuf *buf);
 int nan_ndl_add_ndc_attr(struct nan_data *nan, const struct nan_peer *peer,
